{
  cat <<'EOF'
Sway machine/personal-specific config (extra-* mechanism)

config loads every extra-* snippet under ~/.config/sway/ through
"include extra-*". These snippets hold machine-specific or personal sway
config and are deliberately not tracked in any repository. For example:
  - window rules (float apps like color pickers and password prompts)
  - screen output (resolution, scale, wallpaper)
  - cursor and icon theme

When missing, "include extra-*" is silently ignored by sway, so startup
is unaffected; create them per machine after the first deploy.

Two kinds of machine-specific but almost always needed settings to keep
in mind:
  - polkit authentication agent: lets apps that need root show a
    password dialog, e.g. in extra-autostart:
      exec --no-startup-id /usr/lib/polkit-gnome/polkit-gnome-authentication-agent-1
  - systemd user environment variables: sway does not import DISPLAY /
    WAYLAND_DISPLAY into the systemd user environment on its own; without
    them mako won't autostart and the input-method theme may misbehave.
    On Arch, include /etc/sway/config.d/50-systemd-user.conf (see FS#63021).
EOF
} \
  | while IFS= read -r line; do
      msg "$line"
    done

